cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AG-NAM, its benchmarking framework, or its publication artifacts, please cite this software."
title: "AG-NAM: Attention-Guided Neural Additive Models for Reproducible and Interpretable Feature Interaction Learning"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Cihan"
    given-names: "Mücahit"
version: "1.0.0"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - neural additive models
  - interpretable machine learning
  - feature interactions
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - tabular learning
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  AG-NAM is a reproducibility-aware neural additive modeling framework for
  selective pairwise feature interaction learning. It combines residual-guided
  candidate discovery, repeated-selection reproducibility, Interaction
  Stability Refinement based on purified interaction-surface agreement, and
  fresh final-model training while preserving an explicitly decomposable
  additive predictor.